# Build output. All of it, ignored at the root, because every branch below
# generates some and none of it belongs in the history.
#
# `plugins/` and `proxy/` are cargo workspaces: target/ holds the wasm32 core
# modules and the host-side encoder artifacts, and dist/ holds the components
# those are encoded into. Neither is source. A compiled artifact in a git tree
# is a second copy of something already described by the files beside it, and
# it goes stale silently. `just plugins` builds them; nothing reads them from
# the tree.
target/
plugins/dist/

# nix-direnv caches the dev shell in .direnv/, and `nix build` leaves result
# symlinks; `nix run .#vm` writes a disk and a firmware variable store beside
# wherever it was run.
.direnv/
result
result-*
/losos-desktop.qcow2
/losos-desktop-efivars.fd
